This is the MM/1 OS-9/68000 port of Aladdin Ghostscript ver 3.33.This version is distributed under a license which is NOT the sameas the GNU/FSF license for previous versions.  The license canbe found in the file "PUBLIC" in this archive.                      **************************            The following was copied from the "PUBLIC" file.                            Read the file               ******************************************		ALADDIN GHOSTSCRIPT FREE PUBLIC LICENSE			(Version 4, March 5, 1995)		Copyright (C) 1994, 1995 Aladdin Enterprises,		Menlo Park, California, U.S.A.  All rights reserved.	NOTE: This license is not the same as any of the GNU Licenses	published by the Free Software Foundation.  Its terms are	substantially different from those of the GNU Licenses.	If you are familiar with the GNU Licenses, please read this	license with extra care.                  **********************************This archive contains:gs33 - the Ghostscript programgs_xxx.ps assorted initialization filesfontmap - Ghostscript's font finderxxx.pfb, xxx.gsf (a couple fonts to get you running)use.doc - the instructionspublic - Copyright distrubution infoThe program was compiled on a 9-Meg MM/1a , using theGCC ver 2.5.8 compiler and libraries.  Very few changes were madeto the original source code to get it to compile - complete sourcecan be found on ftp.cs.wisc.edu /ghost/aladdin.  There are over500 files - about 6.7 megs of source, headers, and makefiles.As with previous ports of Ghostscript, I have a Deskjet-500 and anEpson Action Printer 5000 (LQ570).  I was not able to test theother printer drivers, but the fact that the Deskjet, Epson,Dfax and various bitmap drivers worked with NO modifications givesme some confidence.To run Ghostscript, you will need the files in this archive PLUSa "fontmap" file and fonts from previous GS uploads.  If you havethe Adobe Type Manager, or another source of Adobe type fonts,these can be used.  The complete Ghostscript font distributionis also available from the INTERNET source given above.GS33 expects to find the init files, fonts, and fontmap in"/dd/etc/lib/gs33" --OR-- directory indicated in environmentvariable GS_LIB.  Note that an init file from a previousversion of Ghostscript will cause it to choke and quit.Changes from previous versions. Kwindows display is larger and a little faster on some drawings. Printer drivers now direct output to "/p" by default - use the command line switch "-sOUTPUTFILE=(path)" to direct to a file or another device. GS ver 3.33 includes support for several new input and output formats, including JPEG and PDF (Adobe Acrobat) files.  See the file "use.doc" for details. The program gets bigger with every version, but still can be run on a 3-meg MM/1.Undocumented features: An occasional "gift" in the form of an unexpected output filein /dd/tmp - happens after changing output device within theprogram. The colors in the Kwindows display are not always what I expect -It picks the first 16 colors it finds and locks them into thepalette slots - running the "colorcir.ps" demo ahead of the"tiger.ps" demo (for example) will produce a better tiger.